From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: enable r_i2c1 + HUSB311 Type-C port controller

Adds the last piece between "USB3 is alive" and "USB3 is usable". On 2026-07-21
the combo-PHY came up on the 8 GiB board and xhci reported SuperSpeed Plus (LINK_STUS0 =
0x111), J4 VBUS was on (PL2 high, verified via PL_CFG0/PL_DAT), and still nothing
enumerated -- on any bus, not even at USB2. A compliant device only presents its
pull-up once it sees Rp on CC, and with no TCPC driving CC1/CC2 they float.

  - S_TWI1 @ 0x07084000, IRQ GIC_SPI 204 (the interrupt list of the A733 user manual
    intid 236). Read from our spec; the vendor DT happens to agree here, which is
    a cross-check rather than the source.
  - pins PL12/PL13 at mux 3 (the pin tables of the A733 user manual: PL12 = S-TWI1-SCK, PL13 = S-TWI1-SDA).
    Several PL/PM pairs can carry S_TWI1; this is the pair the board wires.
  - U4 = HUSB311 @ 0x4e, IRQ TYPEC_INT = PL3, supply VCC_3V3_TYPEC = SWOUT1
    (190).

No new driver: mainline tcpci_rt1711h matches "richtek,rt1711h", the fallback
compatible the HUSB311 is register-compatible with.

The connector is declared source/host only. `phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy` hard-codes NORMAL lane
orientation because we have no orientation source yet, so advertising dual-role
or a flipped plug would promise more than the PHY can deliver. Once the TCPC
reports orientation, that limit and this property go together.

HW-pending, one observable: the TCPC probes on i2c-1, a device plugged into J4
enumerates, and /sys/bus/usb/devices/*/speed gains an entry beyond the six root
hubs plus hub -- 5000 or 10000 for a SuperSpeed stick.

Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -1611,6 +1611,19 @@
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
 				function = "r_i2c0";
 			};
+
+			/*
+			 * Type-C port controller I2C = S_TWI1 on PL12/PL13.
+			 * the pin tables of the A733 user manual: PL12 sel 3 = S-TWI1-SCK, PL13 sel 3 =
+			 * S-TWI1-SDA -- several PL/PM pairs can carry S_TWI1, this
+			 * is the pair the board wires (schematic; the vendor DT
+			 * agrees, but the spec table is the source here).
+			 */
+			r_i2c1_pins: r-i2c1-pins {
+				pins = "PL12", "PL13";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "r_i2c1";
+			};
 		};
 
 		/*
@@ -1680,6 +1693,112 @@
 				};
 			};
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * S_TWI1 @ 0x07084000 (the memory map of the A733 user manual: SYSCPUS_APBS1,
+		 * 0x07084000-0x07084FFF), IRQ GIC_SPI 204 (S_TWI1 intid 236,
+		 * the interrupt list of the A733 user manual). Both read off our own spec, not copied from
+		 * another SoC -- the same care that caught the A523 r_i2c0
+		 * address landing inside S_UART1 on the A733.
+		 *
+		 * It exists for exactly one consumer: the Type-C port controller.
+		 */
+		r_i2c1: i2c@7084000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun8i-v536-i2c",
+				     "allwinner,sun6i-a31-i2c";
+			reg = <0x0 0x07084000 0x0 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 204 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_I2C1>;
+			resets = <&r_ccu RST_BUS_R_I2C1>;
+			pinctrl-names = "default";
+			pinctrl-0 = <&r_i2c1_pins>;
+			status = "okay";
+
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+
+			/*
+			 * U4 = HUSB311, the USB Type-C port controller on J4's
+			 * CC1/CC2 (
+			 * supply VCC_3V3_TYPEC = SWOUT1, IRQ TYPEC_INT = PL3, ibid
+			 * :190). It does CC detection, orientation and VBUS sense;
+			 * the lane muxing itself happens inside the SoC COMB0 PHY.
+			 *
+			 * Why this node is what makes USB3 usable rather than just
+			 * alive: on 2026-07-21 the combo-PHY came up and xhci
+			 * reported SuperSpeed Plus (LINK_STUS0 = 0x111), J4 VBUS
+			 * was on (PL2 high), and still nothing enumerated -- a
+			 * compliant device only presents its pull-up once it sees
+			 * Rp on CC, and with no TCPC driving CC1/CC2 they float.
+			 *
+			 * No new driver is needed: mainline tcpci_rt1711h matches
+			 * "richtek,rt1711h", which the HUSB311 is register-
+			 * compatible with (same fallback the vendor DT uses).
+			 */
+			typec_pd: usb-pd@4e {
+				compatible = "hynetek,husb311", "richtek,rt1711h";
+				reg = <0x4e>;
+				interrupt-parent = <&r_pio>;
+				interrupts = <0 3 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+				vbus-supply = <&reg_usb3_vbus>;
+				status = "okay";
+
+				usb_con: connector {
+					compatible = "usb-c-connector";
+					label = "USB-C";
+					/*
+					 * Host-only: the board is a DFP here.
+					 * Orientation IS handled -- `phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy` mirrors
+					 * the lanes and TCPM reports the plug
+					 * direction through the graph below.
+					 */
+					power-role = "source";
+					data-role = "host";
+					typec-power-opmode = "default";
+					/*
+					 * No USB-PD policy here, and saying so
+					 * is required rather than optional:
+					 * tcpm_fw_get_caps() sets pd_supported
+					 * from the absence of this property and
+					 * then insists on source-pdos, failing
+					 * probe with -EINVAL. Observed on the 8 GiB board,
+					 * 2026-07-21. We only want Type-C
+					 * attach/Rp so a device connects; PD
+					 * would need a power policy this board
+					 * does not have.
+					 */
+					pd-disable;
+
+					/* The SS lanes are orientation-mirrored
+					 * inside COMB0, so TCPM has to tell the
+					 * combo-PHY which way the plug went in.
+					 * port@1 is that link. port@0 is required
+					 * by the binding whenever `ports` is used
+					 * and is inert here:
+					 * dwc3 only builds a role switch when
+					 * usb-role-switch is set, which it is not.
+					 */
+					ports {
+						#address-cells = <1>;
+						#size-cells = <0>;
+
+						port@0 {	/* High Speed */
+							reg = <0>;
+							usb_con_hs: endpoint {
+								remote-endpoint = <&usb3_hs>;
+							};
+						};
+
+						port@1 {	/* Super Speed */
+							reg = <1>;
+							usb_con_ss: endpoint {
+								remote-endpoint = <&combophy0_ss>;
+							};
+						};
+					};
+				};
+			};
+		};
 
 		/*
 		 * RTC-CCU (PRCM @0x07090000, AON domain). Provides the two SERDES
